# C:\Users\AdityaGollapalli\Downloads\gitcourse>git remote add -u origin https://github.com/adityagepam990/gitcourse.git
# fatal: not a git repository (or any of the parent directories): .git

## This error happens when the repo is not initialised with .git or Git.

### To fix this:
- git init
- git remote add origin https://github.com/adityagepam990/gitcourse.git

-----

# This error happens because your remote repository on GitHub already contains files 
# (for example, if you checked the box to "Add a README file", "Add .gitignore", or "Choose a license" when creating the repository on GitHub), but your local folder doesn't have those files yet.

## You need to pull (fetch and merge) the changes from GitHub to your local machine first. Run the following command:
> git pull origin main --allow-unrelated-histories

+ Once the pull is completed then push it

